$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure 2: To a flask were added phthalide (6 mmol), NBS (7.2
mmol), and AIBN (0.6 mmol) under an argon atmosphere. The mixture was
well mixed with stirring for 2 min. Then the mixture was heated at 60 °C
until the starting phthalide was consumed completely. After one hour,
diethyl ether (15 mL) was added to the mixture, and the obtained mixture
was filtered to remove succinimide. The filtrate was evaporated and the
residue was chromatographed on silica gel (eluent: hexane-ethyl acetate =
1:1) to obtain ethyl α-bromo-p-toluate. Yield 76%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, regioselective, Wohl-Ziegler reaction, ionic
liq. solvent, reaction alternately run with benzoyl peroxide as catalyst
or without solvent with comparable yields
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Environmentally-friendly Wohl-Ziegler bromination: Ionic-liquid reaction
and solvent-free reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Togo, Hideo; Hirai, Takeshi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2003), (5), 702-704

