$DATUM 56-23-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Simultaneous Bromination/Alkylation of Toluene (Route A).
Bromination/Alkylation of Toluene Using Pretreated Heat-Activated Clays.
Montmorillonite K 10 or bentonite (20 g) was suspended in deionized water
(250 mL), stirred rapidly for ca. 10 s, and left standing for ca. 1.5
min. The supernatant slurry was decanted and filtered by suction. The
residue was further washed with deionized water four times before drying
and activation at the required temperature. Toluene (15 mL), optionally
diluted with CCl4 (15 mL) and containing the activated clay (0.30 g), was
treated with diluted molecular bromine (1 g in 15 mL of CCl4) over a
period of 45 min. The reaction was heated at the required temperature for
4 h, the catalyst filtered off, and the reaction mixture analysed by GC.
Benzylbromide, yield 80%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM yield depends on reaction cat.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalysts and Process for the Production of Benzyl Toluenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Barton, Benita; Hlohloza, Nkululeko S.; McInnes, Sonia M.; Zeelie,
Bernard
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2003), 7(4), 571-576

