$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Benzylic Bromides 2a-f; Genearl Procedure NBS
(10.8 g, 60 mmol) was added in three equal portions during 9 h to a
solution of 1 (10 mmol) in refluxing CCl4 (60 mL), each addition being
followed by a few milligrams of benzoyl peroxide. The mixture was cooled
and filtered to remove the succinimide. The filtrate was washed with aq
NaHCO3 solution (30 mL) and brine (30 mL). After drying (Na2SO4), the
solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure and the residue was
dissolved in anhyd THF (20 mL). To the resulting solution were added
diethyl phosphite (15.4 mL, 120 mmol) and i-Pr2NEt (20.8 mL, 120 mmol) at
0 °C under Ar with stirring. The mixture was gradually warmed to r.t. and
stirred for 29 h (the reaction was monitored by 1H NMR). The mixture was
poured into ice/water and extracted with Et2O (3 x 40 mL). The organic
layer was washed with 1 M HCl (except for 2e) and brine, dried (Na2SO4),
filtered and evaporated to give the crude product. The pure product was
obtained by silica gel column chromatography with petroleum ether as
eluent (Tables 1 and 2). 2f, yield 82%. Mp: 116-118°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ,
J Hz: 4.49 (s, 2 H), 7.53 (m, 2 H), 7.66 (dd, 2 H, J = 2.1, 6.6). MS (70
eV, EI) M/z (%): 197 (M + 2, 4), 116 (100), 89 (18). IR (KBr) cm-1: 2225
(C≡ N), 1605, 1504, 1411, 1289, 1230, 1097, 847, 743, 604.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An efficient method for the preparation of benzylic bromides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liu, Peinian; Chen, Yingchun; Deng, Jingen; Tu, Yongqiang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2001), (14), 2078-2080

