$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Preparation Methylarene (1 mmol), BBr3
(1.2 mmol), and 5mL CCl4 were reacted at room temperature in oven-dry
glassware containing a Teflon-coated stirred bar and dry septum under an
argon atmosphere. When the reaction reach the end, as indicated by
thin-layer chromatography (TLC; 25:1 petroleum ether-ethyl acetate), the
mixture was quenched with water and extracted with dichloromethane, and
the organic layer was washed with brine and dried over Na2SO4. The
solvent was evaporated in vacuum, and the crude product was subjected to
column chromatography using 100 to 200-mesh gel as stationary phase and
petroleum ether-ethyl acetate (25:1) as eluent. Finally, the individual
product was received. 6a, yield 81.3%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
