$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM trans-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)(4-bromo-1-naphthyl) 1(BrNap). (A) Complex 2(1-Nap)
(10 mg, 0.013 mmol) in 0.5 mL of C6D6 was placed in a 5 mm quartz NMR
tube. The solution was irradiated with a UV-lamp (450 W mercury vapor
lamp) for 30 min after which time the reddish color had faded to yield a
yellow solution. The volatiles were then removed in vacuo. The residue
was washed with cold hexane and dried in vacuo. Yellow crystals for the
X-ray analysis were obtained by hexane layering of a concentrated CH2Cl2
solution. 1(BrNap). Yield (8.0 mg, 86 %). pale yellow solid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, mercury vapor lamp used (450 W), alternative preparation
shown
