$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of alkylnaphthazarines IIa-IIf
with molecular bromine in CCl4. General procedure. To a solution of 0.2
mmol of naphthazarine in 50 ml of CCl4 was added at room temperature 10
μl of Br2, and the reaction mixture was kept in light within 0.5-24 h. On
completion of the reaction the solvent was removed under a vacuum, the
residue was subjected to preparative TLC (eluent hexane-acetone, 3:1), or
it was recrystallized from ethanol.
2-(1'-Bromoethyl)-5,8-dihydroxy-1,4-naphthoquinone (IIIa). Yield 86%,
dark-red crystals. Time 12-24 hours, room temperature. mp 127-137°C
(127-137°C [4]). IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3050, 1659, 1613, 1571. 1H NMR
spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.99 d (3H, CH3, J 6.8 Hz), 5.47 q.d (1H, H1', J1 6.8,
J2 0.7 Hz), 7.20 s (2H, H6, H7), 7.28 d (1H, H3, J 0.7 Hz), 12.40 s,
12.64 s (2H, α-OH). Mass spectrum, m/z (Irel, %): 296/298 [M]+ (19), 219
[M - Br]+ (100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, regioselective, direct sun light used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chemistry of naphthazarine derivatives: XIV. Preparative synthesis of
1'-bromoalkylnaphthazarines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pokhilo, N. D.; Yakubovskaya, A. Ya.; Anufriev, V. F.; Berdyshev, D. V.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
