$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Tris(bromomethyl) Precursor 5. A mixture of compound 431 (309 mg, 0.88
mmol) and N-bromosuccinimide (917 mg, 5.15 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (50 mL) was
irradiated with a sunlamp under N2 for 24 h and then concentrated to
dryness on a rotary evaporator. The resulting yellow solid was triturated
with methanol to give the product. Palebrown solid (439 mg, 85%). mp 214
°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): 3.92 (s, 6H), 7.46 (s, 15H). 13C NMR (CDCl3,
75 MHz): 30.4, 128.2, 129.6, 135.1, 136.8, 144.0. IR (thin film): 776m,
700m. EI-MS (M+, m/z): found for C27H21Br3, 582/584/586/588.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical (Sunlamp used)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Minimalist Synthetic Host with Stacked Guanidinium Ions Mimics the
Weakened Hydration Shells of Protein-protein Interaction Interfaces
