$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4’-Bromomethyl-biphenyl-2-carbonitrile (5).A suitable reactor was charged
with 4’-methyl-biphenyl-2-carbonitrile 6(200 g, 1.03 mol, GC assay 100%),
48% aqueous hydrobromicacid (0.7 g), and cyclohexane (500 mL), and the
mixture was heated to 67 °C. To the obtained clear solution was added
2,2’-azobisisobutyronitrile (4.2 g, 0.025 mol). A small portion of
suspension containing N-bromosuccinimide (202.8 g, 1.12 mol) in
cyclohexane (500 mL) was added. The reaction mixture turned orange, and a
temperature increase of 1–2 °C was observed, indicating the start of the
reaction. The remaining NBS suspension in cyclohexane was now added in
portions within 2 h at 65–68 °C. The addition funnel was rinsed with
cyclohexane (100 mL), and the reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h at 67
°C and then cooled within 4 h to 20 °C. The mixture was filtered, and the
filter cake was washed with cyclohexane (300 mL), isopropanol (150 mL),
and 65 °C warm water (400 mL). Drying at 60 °C for 20 h gave 244 g of
bromo compound 5 (yield = 85%). Assay (HPLC=98%, with 1–2% nitrile 6 and
<1% of dibromide 7. 4’-Bromomethyl-biphenyl-2-carbonitrile (5), yield
85%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
