$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-Bromo-4-methoxy-1,1,1-trifluoro-3-penten-2-one (5a); Typical Procedure
for Monobrominated Compounds 5a-d, 6a-d, 7a, 8a) To a stirred solution of
1a (3.36 g, 20 mmol) in CHCl3 (25 mL) was added dropwise (1.5 h) bromine
solution (3.4 g, 20 mmol) in CHCl3 (25 mL). The red reaction mixture was
cooled to -10 °C in ice-bath and then added pyridine solution (1.7 g, 20
mmol) in CHCl3 (25 mL). The mixture was stirred for 30 minutes and then
was washed with H2O (3 x 50 mL) and dried (Na2SO4). The solution was
filtered, the solvent evaporated and the product was purified by flash
chromatography [silica (Merck 230-400 mesh); CHCl3-hexane, 4: 2]. Yields,
physical constants and selected spectroscopic data are shown in Table 1.
5c, yield 85%. Molecular Formula: C12H16BrF3O4 ;(M. wt.): 361.14; IR
(KBr), (cm-1): 1695 C=O 1590 C=C; 1H NMR(CDCl3-TMS) δ, J (Hz); 13C
NMR(CDCl3-TMS) δ, JC-F (Hz): 5.50 (s, 1 H, H-3), 5.90 (t, 1 H, H-5, 7.5),
4.00 (s, 3 H, OMe), 3.70 (s, 3 H, CO2Me), 2.30 (t, 2 H, H9, 8.0), 2.00
(m, 2 H H6), 1.70 (m, 2 H, H7), 1.40 (m, 2 H, H8), 116.0 (C-1, 91), 179.0
(C-2), 91.0 (C-3), 176.4 (C-4), 45.2 (C-5), 33.5 (C-6), 25.0 (C-7), 27.0
(C-8), 35.0 (C-9), 173.5 (C-10), 56.5 (OMe), 51.5 (CO2Me)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Regiospecific allylic mono- and dibromination of
4-methoxy-1,1,1-trihalo-3-alken-2-ones and
5-methoxy-1,1,1,2,2-pentafluoro-4-hexen-2-one, and their applications to
the synthesis of heterocycles
