$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Dimethyl 2,5-bis(bromomethyl)benzene-1,4-dicarboxyrate 2.1 A mixture of
dimethyl 2,5-dimethyltelephthalate (20.1 g, 90.6 mmol), NBS (26.8 g, 150
mmol), AIBN (600 mg), and CH2Cl2 (250 mL) was stirred for 2h under
reflux. To the mixture was added NBS (8.92 g, 50.1 mmol) and stirred for
an additional 2h under reflux. After cooling, the mixture was washed with
sat. aqueous NaHCO3, and dried with MgSO4. The filtrate was concentrated
and recrystallized from CH2Cl2/hexane to afford bromide 2 (29.3 g, 85%).
-2: Colorless needles (CH2Cl2/hexane). mp 110-112 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz) δ
3.98 (s, 6H, OCH3), 4.94 (s, 4H, CH2Br), 8.06 (s, 2H, ArH). IR (KBr) ν
1724 (C=O) cm-1.
