$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Bromo-3,4-bis-bromomethyl-2,5-bis-octadecyloxybenzene (7h). A solution
of bromine (3.3 mL, 10.3 g, 64.4 mmol) in CHCl3 (400 mL) was added
dropwise over a 3.5 h period to a solution of 5h (37.2 g, 57.8 mmol) in
CHCl3 (500 mL) at room temperature under argon. After 22 h, the reaction
washed successively with sat aq NaHCO3 (250 mL), sat aq Na2SO3 (250 mL),
and brine (250 mL). The organic phase was dried (MgSO4) and concentrated
under vacuum to a yellow solid, which was purified by crystallization
from absolute EtOH to give 39.4 g (51 mmol, 88%) of 6h as a light yellow
solid that was not characterized. NBS (19.4 g, 109 mmol) was added in one
portion to a solution of 6h (38.3 g, 49.6 mmol) in CCl4 (1 L) under
argon. A 250 W (115 to 125 V) IR heat lamp was positioned near the
reaction flask to ensure a gentle reflux. After 24 h, the solution was
cooled to room temperature, succinimide was removed by filtration, and
the solid was washed with CCl4 (50 mL). The solution was washed
successively with sat aq NaHCO3 (500 mL), sat aq Na2SO3 (500 mL), and
brine (500 mL). The organic phase was dried (MgSO4), filtered, and
concentrated under vacuum to give an orange residue. The residue was
triturated with hot acetonitrile to afford 7h.
1-Bromo-3,4-bis-bromomethyl-2,5-bis-octadecyloxybenzene (7h), light
yellow solid, yield 42.4 g, 48.2 mmol, 85% (for two steps). Rf 0.90 (10%
EtOAc/hexanes), mp 53-56 °C. IR (KBr) cm-1 1468, 1252, 1085; 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.86 (6H, t, J = 6.1 Hz), 1.24 (56H, m), 1.49 (4H, m), 1.83
(4H, septet, J = 7.3 Hz), 3.95 (2H, t, J = 6.2 Hz), 4.02 (2H, t, J = 6.5
Hz), 4.69 (2H, s), 4.70 (2H, s), 7.02 (1H, s); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
14.1, 22.7, 23.4, 23.7, 25.9, 26.0, 29.1, 29.3, 29.4, 29.5, 29.7, 30.0,
31.9, 69.1, 74.2, 117.2, 118.4, 125.9, 132.7, 148.6, 153.7; HRMS (FAB+)
cacld for C44H7979Br3O2 (M+) 876.3630, found 876.3609 (-2.4 ppm).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, IR heat lamp used (250 W) (stage 2), dropwise addn. of a
slight excess of reagent (in CHCl3) (stage 1, substage 1), selective for
ring-monobromination (stage 1) and side chain bromination (stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic crystal engineering with 1,4-piperazine-2,5-diones. 8. Synthesis,
crystal packing, and thermochemistry of piperazinediones derived from
2-amino-4,7-dialkoxyindan-2-carboxylic acids
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
