$DATUM β-Hexabromo-meso-tris[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]subporphyrin (4b) From
subporphyrin 2b (30 mg, 43 μmol), chromatography (CH2Cl2-PE-Et2O,
1:20:1), to give 4b (41 mg, 82%) as a yellow solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3, -40 °C): δ = 8.28 (d, J = 7.80 Hz, 3 H, o-HPh), 8.04 (d, J = 7.80
Hz, 3 H, m-HPh), 7.78 (d, J = 7.80 Hz, 3 H, m-HPh), 7.41 (d, J = 7.80 Hz,
3 H, o-HPh). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 135.51, 134.44, 133.48,
132.87, 132.44, 132.11, 131.79, 131.46, 128.22, 125.50, 125.10, 124.53,
122.79, 120.08, 118.75, 118.65. 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -62.30 (s,
9 F, CF3), -156.83 (m, 1 F, BF). HRMS (MALDI TOF): m/z [M-F]+ calcd for
C36H12BN3F9Br6: 1140.6190; found: 1140.6163. UV/Vis (CH2Cl2): λ (relative
intensity) = 468 (17.5), 456 (2.2), 478 nm (1). Fluorescence (CH2Cl2, λex
= 368 nm): λmax = 517, 486 nm, ΦF = 0.002.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM literature preparation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
