$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Trimethylsilyl 4-Bromo-2-alkenoates (3): In
the device described above are placed the trimethylsilyl 2-alkenoate (2;
0.5 mol), N-bromosuccinimide (107 g, 0.6 mol; for 2d only 71.2 g, 0.4
mol), dibenzoyl peroxide (2 g), and tetrachloromethane (650 ml). The
mixture is stirred for 15 min at room temperature then refluxed under
irradiation with visible light until the suspension rises to the surface
(∼3 h). The flask is cooled on ice and the floating succinimide is
filtered off. The filtrate is concentrated under reduced pressure and the
crude product distilled in vacuum. Trimethylsilyl 4-Bromo-2-alkenoate
(3d). Yield: 81 %. b.p.: found: 60-70 °C/0.2 torr, molecular formula:
C8H15BrSiO2 (251.2).
