$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1,1,3-Tribromo-2-(bromomethyl)prop-1-ene
(2aa); Typical Procedure In a 250 mL three-necked flask, fitted with a
stirrer, N2 inlet tube and reflux condenser were placed
1,1-dibromo-2-methylprop-1-ene (3a;10 g, 0.0472 mol), N-bromosuccinimide
(16.2 g, 0.092 mol), benzoyl peroxide (1.7 g, 15 mol%) (Caution!),11 and
CCl4 (100 mL). The mixture was stirred at reflux under N2 for 2 h (The
consumption of the starting material was monitored by 1H NMR spectra).
After filtration, the succinimide formed was washed with CCl4 (2 × 30
mL). Rotary evaporation and flash chromatography on silica gel (eluent:
petroleum ether) afforded 2aa 1,1,3-Tribromo-2-(bromomethyl)pent-1-ene
(2cc) Compound 3c (0.137 g, 0.57 mmol), NBS (0.206 g, 1.16 mmol) and BPO
(0.02 g, 0.083 mmol) afforded 2cc. 0.184 g (81%). mp 64 °C. 1H NMR: δ =
5.17 (t, J = 7.41 Hz, 1 H), 4.29 (d, J = 10.65 Hz, 1 H), 4.23 (d, J=
10.65 Hz, 1 H), 1.97-2.28 (m, 2 H), 1.08 (t, J = 7.21 Hz, 3 H). 13C NMR:
δ = 140.204, 99.495, 56.932, 30.687, 28.945, 12.954. IR (KBr): ν =1568,
1436, 1266, 1214, 1134, 1104 cm-1. MS: m/z (%) = 404 [M+ (4 × 81Br),
0.30], 402 [M+ (3 × 81Br, 1 × 79Br), 1.40], 400 [M+ (2 × 81Br, 2 × 79Br),
1.74], 398 [M+ (1 × 81Br, 3 × 79Br), 1.28], 396 [M+ (4 × 79Br), 0.52], 79
(Br+, 100.00). Anal. calcd for C6H8Br4: C, 18.03; H, 2.02. Found: C,
17.85; H, 1.77.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM product depends on stoichiometry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stepwise α-bromination of 1,1-dihalo alkenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ma, Sheng Ming; Xu, Bin; Zhao, Shi Min
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2000), (1), 139-143

