$DATUM 75-05-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Monobromides 3a-l; General Procedure. To a
soln of the 1,3,5,7-tetramethyl-BODIPY 1 (0.2 mmol) and K2CO3 (0.6 mmol)
in anhyd MeCN (20 mL) was slowly added a soln of CuBr2 (0.3 mmol) in MeCN
(25 mL). The mixture was stirred under an O2 atmosphere (balloon) at r.t.
for 24 h. The residue obtained after the removal of the solvent by rotary
evaporation was extracted with EtOAc (3 × 40 mL), and the extracts were
washed with H2O (3 × 30 mL), dried (anhyd Na2SO4), and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude product was further purified using column
chromatography (EtOAc-petroleum ether) afforded compound.
2-Bromo-4,4-difluoro-1,3,5,7-tetramethyl-8-phenyl-4-bora-3a,4a-diaza-s-indacene
(3a). Yield: 65.3 mg (81%); red solid. mp 183-185 °C. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 1.38 (s, 3 H, CH3), 1.40 (s, 3 H, CH3), 2.59 (s, 3 H, CH3),
2.61 (s, 3 H, CH3), 6.05 (s, 1 H, pyrrole-H), 7.25-7.30 (m, 2 H, ArH),
7.49-7.55 (m, 3 H, ArH). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 157.9, 151.4,
145.1, 141.8, 138.8, 134.7, 132.0, 129.8, 129.3, 127.9, 122.2, 14.8,
14.5, 13.4. EI-MS: m/z = 402 [M - H]+. Anal. Calcd for C19H18BBrF2N2: C,
56.62; H, 4.50; N, 6.95. Found: C, 56.60; H, 4.55; N, 6.91.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, 3 equiv. of K2CO3 used, optimized on base,stoichiometry,
product depends on stoichiometry and additive, oxygen (balloon) used,
optimization study, 1.5 equiv. of CuBr2 used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An efficient and convenient bromination of BODIPY derivatives with
copper(II) bromide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ye, Jia-Hai; Wang, Guangpu; Huang, Chengmei; Hu, Zhengjuan; Zhang,
Whenchao; Zhang, Yan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2012), 44(1), 104-110

