$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.3 Synthesis of (αE)-α-methoxyimino-2-(1-bromomethyl)phenylacetate (5)
2.07 g (10 mmol) compound 4 was dissolved in carbon tetrachloride, 2.14 g
(12 mmol) NBS added and a small amount of 2,2'-azobisisobutyronitrile
(AIBN) used as initiator. After refluxed for 12 h, a white solid floated
on the liquid surface, and the reaction was then ceased. The hot solution
was filtered, washed with carbon tetrachloride and concentrated under
reduced pressure to leave a brownish viscous liquid, which was further
purified by silica gel column chromatography (n-hexane/ethyl acetate =
20/1, V/V) to give product 5 (2.32 g, yield 81 %).
(αE)-α-methoxyimino-2-(1-bromomethyl)phenylacetate (5), 81 %, brownish
viscous liquid 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 3.86 (s, 3H, COOMe), 4.04 (s,
3H, N-OCH3), 4.31 (s, 2H, CH2), 7.13 (dd, J1 = 7.8 Hz, J2 = 1.2 Hz, 1H,
3-ArH), 7.35-7.40 (m, 2H, 2 × ArH), 7.46 (dd, J1 = 7.8 Hz, J2 = 0.6 Hz,
1H, 6-ArH); IR (KBr) ν: 2942, 1728 (C=O), 1438, 1321, 1220, 1067, 1018,
958, 762 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoselective synthesis and biological properties of
(αE,E)-α-methoxymino-2-[(1-arylalkylidene)aminooxymethyl]benzeneacetates
