$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Compounds V-XIII. General procedure. To a
mixture of 0.1 mol of olefin and 80 mL of tetrachloromethane was added
NBS [0.105 (V, VIII, IX), 0.21 (VI, XII, XIII), 0.3 mol (VII)] and 1 mmol
of AIBN. The reaction mixture was refluxed at constant stirring for 3
(V), 5 (VI), 15 (VII, XII, XIII), and 20 h (VIII, IX). The succinimide
was filtered off, the filtrate was washed with 20 mL of water and dried
with anhydrous Na2SO4. Tetrachloromethane was evaporated on a rotary
evaporator in a vacuum. (E)-1-(1-Adamantyl)-3-bromoprop-1-ene (V).
Reaction product was distilled in a vacuum at 150°C (10 mm Hg). Yield
80%, light-yellow oil. nD20 1.5415. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 2904 (CHAd),
2846 (CHAd), 1654 (C═C), 1450 (CH2), 1203, 1099, 964 (CH═CH, trans), 786,
640, 578. 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.55-1.73 m (12H, 6CH2Ad), 1.95-2.02 m
(3H, 3CHAd), 3.95 d (2H, CH2Br, J 7.3 Hz), 5.51 d.t (1H, ═CH-CH2, J 15.6,
7.3 Hz), 5.60 d (1H, ═CH, J 15.6 Hz). 13C NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 28.38,
34.54, 34.97, 36.83, 41.87, 121.63, 147.28. Mass spectrum, m/z (Irel, %):
254 (8)[M]+, 175 (100), 147 (5), 135 (11), 133 (13), 119 (15), 117 (18),
105 (16), 93 (24), 91 (37), 79 (31), 77 (20), 55 (15). Found, %: C 61.07;
H 7.64. C13H19Br. Calculated, %: C 61.18; H 7.50. M 255.19.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM products depend on stoichiometry of reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reaction of adamantane series olefins with N-bromosuccinimide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
