$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl 5-bromomethyl-4-(1,2,3-thiadiazol-4-yl) furan-2-carboxylate (5).
The mixture of 2.2 g (9 mmol) of thiadiazole 4, 1.8 g (10 mmol) of NBS,
80 mL of carbon tetrachloride, and 0.1 g of AIBN was refluxed with
stirring for 1.5 h until the disappearance of NBS crystals, and was left
overnight. On the next day succinimide was filtered off, and the filtrate
was evaporated to dryness. The residue was triturated with hexane, the
crystals formed were filtered off and crystallized from ethanol. Yield
2.3 g (78%), orange crystals. Mp 85°C, R f 0.6 (chloroform). 1H NMR
spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm: 1.43 t (3H, CH3CH2O, J HH 7.2 Hz), 4.43 q (2H,
CH3CH2O, J HH 7.2 Hz), 5.02 s (2H, CH2Br), 7.56 s (1H, H3-furan), 8.67 s
(1H, H5-thiadiazole). 13C NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δC, ppm: 14.27 (CH3CH2O),
22.04 (CH2Br), 61.62 (CH3CH2O), 116.93 (C4-furan), 117.81 (C3-furan),
131.84 (C5-furan), 145.00 (C4-thiadiazole), 151.87 (C5-furan), 153.94
(C2-furan), 158.05 (C=O). Mass spectrum, m/z (I rel, %): 318 (3) [M+1],
289 (6), 237 (73), 209 (40), 195 (6), 181 (100), 165 (2), 153 (10), 135
(12), 108 (16), 93 (13), 82 (16), 69 (21), 63 (30), 51 (28), 43 (35), 29
(93).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of ethyl
4-(1,2,3-thiadiazol-4-yl)-5-(bromomethyl)furan-2-carboxylate and its
reactions with nucleophiles
